<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      It will suffice to prove that for every object $Z \rightarrow \calC $ of $(\sSet )_{/\calC }$, the fiber product $Z \times _{\calC } \calC ^{/C}$ is a homotopy product of $Z$ with $\calC ^{/C}$ in $(\sSet )_{/\calC }$ (with respect to the covariant model structure). Choose a factorization 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  Z \stackrel{i}{\rightarrow } Z' \stackrel{j}{\rightarrow } \calC , \]
</div>
    <p>
       where $i$ is left anodyne and $j$ is a left fibration. According to Corollary <a href="/tag/87991F" data-tag="87991F">2.2.3.12</a>, we may regard $Z'$ as a fibrant replacement for $Z$ in $(\sSet )_{/\calC }$. It therefore suffices to prove that the map $i': Z \times _{\calC } \calC ^{/C} \rightarrow Z' \times _{\calC } \calC ^{/C}$ is a covariant equivalence. According to Proposition <a href="/tag/43E46F" data-tag="43E46F">4.1.2.5</a>, it will suffice to prove that $i'$ is left anodyne. The map $i'$ is a base change of $i$ by the projection $p: \calC ^{/C} \rightarrow \calC $; it therefore suffices to prove that $p^{op}$ is smooth. This follows from Proposition <a href="/tag/B9BB9A" data-tag="B9BB9A">4.1.2.14</a>, since $p$ is a right fibration of simplicial sets. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>